+- Durable implementation conclusion:
+  - the active critic explicit height-patch path now supports:
+    - `terrain.height_patch_scheme = "body_single"`
+    - `terrain.height_patch_scheme = "three_body_separate"`
+  - default behavior remains the original single-patch mode:
+    - one patch referenced to the middle-body root frame
+  - in `three_body_separate` mode:
+    - three patches are sampled independently using the same local patch grid
+    - the reference origins are the COMs of:
+      - `head_car_chassis`
+      - `body_car_chassis`
+      - `tail_car_chassis`
+    - each patch is rotated by its own body yaw
+    - each patch height is expressed relative to its own body COM height
+    - the final critic height vector is concatenated in:
+      - `head -> body -> tail`
+  - `terrain.get_num_height_points()` now returns the total concatenated dimension implied by the selected scheme
+- Reason:
+  - the user explicitly required keeping the current middle-body patch method while adding an alternative scheme that builds three yaw-aligned local patches around the front, middle, and rear body COMs and concatenates them into the critic observation
+- Impact:
+  - future Stage1 terrain-patch experiments can switch schemes only by changing `terrain.height_patch_scheme` in config
+  - observation-dimension checks for critic terrain features must now account for either one patch or three concatenated patches depending on the selected scheme
+- Status:
+  - targeted `python3 -m py_compile` check passed for the modified direct-workflow files
